stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> fresh_state
    fresh_state --> scope
    scope --> design_choices
    design_choices --> verified
    verified --> honest_state
    honest_state --> threshold
    threshold --> checks_green
    threshold --> stalled
    checks_green --> reported
    stalled --> reported
    reported --> [*]

    fresh_state    : Re-read the PR (gh pr view --json state,mergedBy,headRefOid) and fetch the base branch; confirm it is still open and nothing changed since your last look
    scope          : Ask Kev whether to keep, split or grow the PR; move every unrelated change into its own PR
    design_choices : Put each non-obvious naming, layout or scope decision to Kev as its own choice question; hand near-ties to the user
    verified       : Verify the change end to end in the real runtime: run the tests, run the repo CI gates locally, deploy to a dev environment where the repo requires it
    honest_state   : Build the Kev state from verified facts only; list unverified items plainly, write criteria neutrally, add no hypothetical facts
    threshold      : Ask Kev for the merge noul; probe one noul per concern, fix the highest first, re-ask until it reaches 0.8 (own PR) or 0.95 (colleague PR with your fix PR applied)
    checks_green   : Get every check green, required or not; merge without administrator bypass
    stalled        : Stop this merge; record the open question on the PR with Kev's scores; ask Kev about other in-scope tasks and do those that reach 0.8
    reported       : Report Kev's scores for every round in the PR body or final summary
